  "worked_solution": "To calculate the $y$-intercept, we need to substitute $x=0$ in the equation of the ellipse and try to solve the resulting equation for $y.$ We do this and solve the resulting equation by completing the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8x-4y+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(0)^{2}+{y}^{2}-8(0)-4y+4 & =0 \\\\ {y}^{2}-4y+4 & =0 \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =0 \\\\ y-2 & =0 \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the ellipse intercepts the $y$-axis at the point $(0,2).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14095453/assets/d2e5f3fc609249eda5a995005e462f3ba1b36a97fd5027de480b9f04c9705fb0.png)",
